Because $P$ is equidistant from each of the vertices of the octahedron, $P$ is the center of the octahedron.  Thus, the distance from $P$ to any vertex is half the length of the edge.  Therefore, $7$ is half the length of the edge of the octahedron, or $14$ times its length.  In particular, the length of the face from $P$ to the sixth vertex is $\boxed{\frac{14}{2} = 7}$.ﯭ
